TIP:  Don’t be put off by the (maj7) chords, they’re easy to play.  (Cmaj7) is just (C) without the index finger.  And (Fmaj7) will always follow the (Cmaj7) so all you do from the (Cmaj7) is keep the finger placement just like it is but drop down one string-set, kind of like you’re playing a (C) and then add your pinky above the ring finger (you can even omit adding the ring finger if you want).  Easy!  You can also play an (F) instead of the (Dm7) on the last line of the verse if you're more comfortable.


